 <td>ZAMSON</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MATRIX LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,645.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MATRIX PH</td>\n                <td>₦1,690.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MATRIX WARRI</td>\n                <td>₦1,690.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>FYNEFIELD</td>\n                <td>₦1,695.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,700.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SAHARA ONNE</td>\n                <td>₦1,685.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MENJ</td>\n                <td>₦1,640.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Nigeria Hits Aviation Fuel Milestone With Zero Jet A-1 Imports in 13 Months\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria has eliminated its dependence on imported aviation fuel for the first time in decades. Domestic refineries supplied the country's entire Jet A-1 market for 13 consecutive months. The development marks a watershed moment for Nigeria's downstream petroleum sector.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nigeria-hits-aviation-fuel-milestone-with-zero-jet-a-1-imports-in-13-months\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    NMDPRA Nears Launch of E10 Petrol Pilot in Lagos, Abuja\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Nigerian Midstream and Downstream Petroleum Regulatory Authority (NMDPRA) has stated that preparations for the national E10 pilot programme are in their final stages. The scheme is set to assess technical, operational, and regulatory readiness ahead of a wider rollout of ethanol-blended petrol.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nmdpra-nears-launch-of-e10-petrol-pilot-in-lagos-abuja\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Sink for Fourth Consecutive Day as U.S.-Iran Tensions Continue to Ease\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude traded at $87.11 per barrel, down 1.41 per cent. West Texas Intermediate (WTI) slipped 1.28 per cent to $81.55 per barrel. The latest decline came after a fourth consecutive night passed without fresh attacks by either Washington or Tehran.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-sink-for-fourth-consecutive-day-as-us-iran-tensions-continue-to-ease\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Cooking Gas Prices Fall Further as Massive LPG Imports Boost Supply\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria's cooking gas market is showing stronger signs of price moderation as increased imports continue to boost product availability. Recent market checks indicate that retail LPG prices have declined steadily across parts of Abuja over the past three weeks.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/cooking-gas-prices-fall-further-as-massive-lpg-imports-boost-supply\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Depot Fuel Prices Hold Firm Despite Nearly 7% Drop in Global Crude Oil\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                     Depot fuel prices across Nigeria remained unchanged on Monday despite a nearly 7 percent decline in global crude oil prices. Checks by Petroleumprice.ng showed that depot prices remained stable across major supply locations. The stable depot pricing means marketers and bulk buyers continue to purchase products at the same rates.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/depot-fuel-prices-hold-firm-despite-nearly-7-drop-in-global-crude-oil\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
